---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import ArrowLink from '../components/ArrowLink.astro';
import {places} from '../data/places';
---
<Base description="Follow the water through Swat Valley: mountain landscapes, living languages and archaeological ground." section="home">
<div class="hero-meta"><span>Swat Valley · Khyber Pakhtunkhwa · Pakistan</span><span>Landscape / memory / life</span></div>
<section class="home-hero"><Photo id="lake" eager detail={false} sizes="100vw"/><h1>SWAT</h1><span class="urdu" lang="ur" dir="rtl">سوات</span><div class="hero-bottom"><h2>A valley,<br/>in many currents.</h2><div><p>Follow the water. Read the stones.<br/>Listen to a living place.</p><ArrowLink href="/atlas/" label="Enter the valley"/></div></div></section>
<div class="hero-credit"><span>Mahodand Lake · Photograph by Murtaza Mahmud</span><a href="/sources/#photo-lake">Image & license ↗</a><span>Begin upstream ↓</span></div>
<section class="home-intro"><div class="marginal"><span class="eyebrow">One valley.<br/>Many ways of seeing.</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:60px">≈</span></div><div><h2>A river runs through it.<br/>So does a world.</h2><p>From the upper branches around Kalam to the inhabited plains near Barikot, Swat holds many landscapes together. Forest, water, excavated stone and everyday life occupy the same valley.</p><p>This is an invitation to look beyond a single view: to follow connections between places, and to meet the sources that help us understand them.</p></div></section>
<section class="atlas-invitation dark"><div><span class="eyebrow">A geographical encounter</span><h2>Follow<br/>the current.</h2><p>Seven places. Three ways of looking. Move between landscape, language and memory without losing your place in the valley.</p><ArrowLink href="/atlas/" label="Open the living atlas"/></div><div class="river-index">{places.map(p=><a href={`/atlas/?place=${p.id}`}><span>{p.name}</span><small>{p.coordinates[1].toFixed(2)}° N ↗</small></a>)}<p class="caption">An index of places · Open the atlas for geographical positions</p></div></section>
<section class="story-section"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">The valley holds more than a view</span><h2>Look a little closer.</h2></div><span class="eyebrow">Two ways into Swat</span></div><div class="story-grid"><div><a class="story-link" href="/heritage/"><Photo id="butkara" detail={false}/><span class="eyebrow">Stone / time / traces</span><h3>The ground remembers.</h3><p>Walk through the evidence of Butkara and Barikot. Read a landscape that has been built and rebuilt.</p><span class="underlink">Enter deep time ↗</span></a></div><a class="story-link" href="/culture/"><div class="culture-block"><div class="words">Pashto<br/>Torwali · Gawri</div><span class="tiny">Language is carried by people.</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Language / making / belonging</span><h3>A valley of voices.</h3><p>Names, music, knowledge and craft: living culture is made again in the present.</p><span class="underlink">Meet the sources ↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="environment-tease"><div><span class="eyebrow">A changing landscape</span><h2>Water leaves a trace.</h2><p>A river connects what happens upstream with life below. Read dated research on floods, forests and the less visible changes within a lake.</p></div><ArrowLink href="/environment/" label="Read the landscape"/></section>
<section class="place-index"><span class="eyebrow">Place notes</span><nav class="place-index-list" aria-label="Place notes">{places.map(p=><a href={`/places/${p.id}/`}>{p.name} ↗</a>)}</nav></section>
</Base>
